From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] manager: keep Wake-on-LAN devices that are still activated after wake

NetworkManager skips Wake-on-LAN/WLAN devices when the system goes to sleep
so they stay armed, but then takes every such device down when the system
wakes up and activates it again. A Wi-Fi device whose driver keeps the
association across suspend (or an Ethernet device that keeps its carrier)
therefore loses the link right after resume and needs a full reconnect.

When such a device is still activated at wake, keep it and only refresh its
dynamic IP configuration, as already done for software devices. Devices that
lost their link are handled as before.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
--- a/src/core/nm-manager.c
+++ b/src/core/nm-manager.c
@@ -7370,8 +7370,24 @@
                 if (nm_device_is_software(device))
                     continue;
 
-                /* Belatedly take down Wake-on-LAN devices; ideally we wouldn't have to do this
-                 * but for now it's the only way to make sure we re-check their connectivity.
+                if (device_is_wake_on_lan(priv->platform, device)
+                    && nm_device_get_state(device) == NM_DEVICE_STATE_ACTIVATED) {
+                    /* The device was armed for wake and is still activated: its
+                     * link (Wi-Fi association or carrier) survived the sleep.
+                     * Keep it and only refresh the dynamic IP configuration and
+                     * connectivity, like for software devices. A link lost while
+                     * asleep is reported by the device and handled as usual.
+                     */
+                    _LOGD(LOGD_SUSPEND,
+                          "sleep: device %s has wake-on-lan and is still activated, keeping it",
+                          nm_device_get_ip_iface(device));
+                    nm_device_update_dynamic_ip_setup(device, "wake up");
+                    continue;
+                }
+
+                /* Belatedly take down other Wake-on-LAN devices; ideally we wouldn't have
+                 * to do this but for now it's the only way to make sure we re-check their
+                 * connectivity.
                  */
                 if (device_is_wake_on_lan(priv->platform, device))
                     nm_device_set_unmanaged_by_flags(device,
